.IX Title "Lucy::Search::ANDQuery 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Search::ANDQuery 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Search::ANDQuery \- Intersect multiple result sets.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 5
\&    my $foo_and_bar_query = Lucy::Search::ANDQuery\->new(
\&        children => [ $foo_query, $bar_query ],
\&    );
\&    my $hits = $searcher\->hits( query => $foo_and_bar_query );
\&    ...
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
ANDQuery is a composite Query which matches
only when all of its children match, so its result set is the intersection
of their result sets.  Documents which match receive a summed score.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 3
\&    my $foo_and_bar_query = Lucy::Search::ANDQuery\->new(
\&        children => [ $foo_query, $bar_query ],
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Create a new ANDQuery.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBchildren\fR \- An array of child Queries.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS make_compiler
.IX Subsection "make_compiler"
.Vb 5
\&    my $compiler = $and_query\->make_compiler(
\&        searcher    => $searcher,     # required
\&        boost       => $boost,        # required
\&        subordinate => $subordinate,  # default: false
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Abstract factory method returning a Compiler derived from this Query.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBsearcher\fR \- A Searcher.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBboost\fR \- A scoring multiplier.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBsubordinate\fR \- Indicates whether the Query is a subquery (as
opposed to a top-level query).  If false, the implementation must
invoke \fBnormalize()\fR on the newly minted Compiler object before returning
it.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Search::ANDQuery isa Lucy::Search::PolyQuery isa Lucy::Search::Query isa Clownfish::Obj.
